{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The untrusted model never sees candidate code, the reference solution, or any secret input. It sees the problem statement and the public tests, and writes prose.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Why the trusted model runs at low reasoning.} At high reasoning it is already a very strong monitor here \u8212- it flags nearly everything. A near-perfect baseline leaves no room for an improvement to show up, so we handicap it to create a measurable gap. This also matches the premise of AI control: the model you {\i trust} is not the model you would pick for capability.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 2.3 How the tests are made and run\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Three model calls per task:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab {\b Plan} \u8212- untrusted model, prose only.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab {\b Implement} \u8212- trusted model turns the plan into runnable {\f1 prop_*} functions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab {\b Pick inputs} \u8212- trusted model writes up to 60 candidate trigger inputs, from the problem statement alone.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each candidate then runs in a fresh temporary directory as a separate Python process: 300 s per candidate, 6 s per call. This is a {\b timeout boundary, not an isolation boundary} \u8212- no rlimits, no container, parent environment inherited.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 An assertion failure is a {\b catch}. A crash is not. The score is {\b binary}: a property fired (1.0), or none did (0.0).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b On \u8220"trigger search\u8221".} Only step 3 above \u8212- the trusted model listing inputs from the problem statement. The codebase also has AST constant mining and coverage-guided fuzzing, but {\b none of it ran} ({\f1 --code-aware-search} is off by default). Richer search is untested here, not shown to be worse.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 2.4 Two PBT arms. We report the deployable one.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Before scoring, every property is checked against the {\b reference} solution:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab An input the reference cannot run is discarded \u8212- it tells us nothing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab On the remaining inputs, a property that fires, errors, or crashes on the reference is {\b unsound}. It complains about correct code, so it generates false alarms.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 That check produces two scores:\par}
